  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nUnsettled weather is expected to continue for the next several days \nas a boundary/front stalls near or just east of the coast. Moisture \nwill continue to stream into the area, continuing medium to high \nchances of rain on Sunday. By Monday, the boundary will start a slow \nmove to the east as a shortwave approaches, confining most of our \nrain chances over the waters. Another boundary will approach by the \nmiddle of the week, but there is a lot of uncertainty in how this \nwill play out. We will continue to watch this, but would not be \nsurprised to see rain chances return as the boundary approaches. \n\nTemperatures will remain a bit cooler through early next week, \nbefore they begin a slow warm-up back into the low 90s. \n\nDue to the persistent northeasterly flow enhancing the Ekman \ntransport mechanism and increasing 7-8 second swell periods, minor \ncoastal flooding is worth monitoring this weekend, especially during \nhigh tide at night into the early morning hours.",
